    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "NEW RECORD FOR THE SWEDE? Stockholm auction house Bukowskis is auctioning off Hilma af Klint’s abstract painting Ser III No on November 19 with an estimate of $600,000 to $800,000, which could break an auction record for the artist, reported The Art Newspaper . The painting was acquired by a private collector in 1995 after the Hilma af Klint Foundation deaccessioned the artwork. In March, the artist’s Vid ankdammen sold for $54,000 at Christie’s and another work, The Power of the Spleen , sold for $165,825 at Stockholm’s Auktionsverk in 2019. Only two abstract paintings from the artist have been sold at auction in more than three decades, according to Louise Wrede, the head of Bukowskis art department. The artist’s foundation is tightly controlled by her nephew and heir, Erik af Klint.",
